nodes.body:
@coderabbitai Regarding the two SFT epoch-boundary comments in [this review](https://github.com/verl-project/verl/pull/8056#pullrequestreview-5708070601):

Thanks for pointing this out. The epoch-boundary resume issue behind this case is addressed in #7974. That PR avoids restoring an exhausted SFT dataloader state at an epoch boundary, allowing the following epoch to run normally and reach the existing blocking final save.

I reproduced the issue in both SPMD and Ray loops and verified #7974’s boundary-restoration logic in an isolated CPU harness with real StatefulDataLoader and mocked training/I/O. #7974 has not yet been merged or integrated into this PR, so the issue remains reproducible on the current head.

